      "category": "security",
      "title": "Exploiting System Management Mode with a very long interrupt",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/smiiiiiiiiiiiiiiii",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49245491",
      "score": 172,
      "comments": 74,
      "author": "WhiteDawn",
      "published": "2026-08-10T16:03:14Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Long-running x86 instructions can disrupt System Management Interrupt timing, exposing race conditions in low-level CPU SMM entry mechanisms.",
        "Exploiting SMM timing flaws enables Ring 0 attackers to execute code in Ring -2, bypassing hypervisor restrictions and Secure Boot.",
        "Mitigations require vendor firmware updates enforcing hardware-assisted SMI synchronization, SMRAM protection locks, and instruction execution limits."
      ]
    },
